Scope
The approval entry takes an optional integer fileVersion of 1 or more. With the field, the writer
delivers <row id>-v2.png and <row id>-line-v2.png. I audited input validation, name escape,
duplicate names, refusal order, partial writes, symlinks, secret handling, and the A2 and A6 rules.

Name escape
deliveredNames requires the suffix /-v\d+\.png$/ on both list names and replaces only that suffix.
The color name also passes planPictureRow, which enforces ^l2-w\d{2}-[a-z-]+-v\d+\.png$. A
JavaScript number string holds no '/' and no '..', so no fileVersion value adds a folder part.

Duplicate names
One map holds both delivered names of every row and refuses a name that another row delivers.
A v2 row cannot take another row's list name in the same run.

Validation
fileVersion is z.number().int().min(1). A string, a fraction, 0, and a negative value are refused
with no coercion. The refusal names entries.0.fileVersion and happens in parseApprovals, before
the first read.

Refusal order and partial writes
The order is: schema, row ids, list pin, names and duplicates, print reads and structural checks,
manifest compare, target file compare, then mkdir and the wx writes. A refusal leaves no file.

Symlinks and bytes
The writer still refuses a symlink at a target, a different manifest.json, and a file with
different bytes, all before mkdir.

Secrets
The change adds no network call, no credential, and no environment read. The new messages hold a
row id and a list file name only. I opened no .env.local file.

A2: not triggered. No draft to published transition. The approval entry is the gate, and
fileVersion does not bypass it.
A6: measure/tracks.md lists the track as [~] with no security-resolved claim. The plan evidence
claims 178 passing tests, and the Green log matches. contract.md line 20 is stale (RB11-03).

Findings (all nonblocking)
RB11-01 Low: fileVersion is not bounded to a safe integer (src/storytime/muse-delivery.ts:69).
  1e21 passes .int().min(1) and gives the name l2-w01-nut-v1e+21.png, which leaves the list
  pattern (src/storytime/book-pictures.ts:1457). No escape and no collision. assertVersion
  (src/storytime/book-pictures.ts:477) already holds the bound.
RB11-02 Nit: the writer checks the line name for a plain name and for manifest.json, and it never
  checks the color name (src/storytime/muse-delivery.ts:366-369). The color name is safe through
  planPictureRow and the prefix-preserving replace. The check is implied, not asserted.
RB11-03 Nit: contract.md line 20 still says the delivered names come from the list and the
  pipeline derives no slug (contract.md:20-23). f1e797cb updates no contract bullet.
RB11-04 Nit: a v2 run into a folder that holds v1 files and no manifest.json leaves the v1 files
  beside the new v2 files. The manifest names only the v2 files.

Test evidence and probe limit
jr-green-v2-delivery.log records vitest exit 0 with 178 passed (178) across the four files, tsc
exit 2 with 0 owned errors, and a mutation proof. This review tried the heavy-run command and a
direct vitest run, and the shell tool refused both with "Permission denied: shell". The verdict
rests on code reading and the Green log. No probe wrote a file.

